<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The adaptive icon: three layers, no bitmaps anywhere.

    There are no PNG mipmaps in this project, and nothing is missing. Adaptive
    icons arrived in API 26 and minSdk here is 26, so every device that can
    install this app can render this file. The usual pile of
    mipmap-{m,h,xh,xxh,xxxh}dpi/ic_launcher.png exists to serve API 25 and
    below, which is not a target.

    There is also no android:roundIcon in the manifest, deliberately. It was
    added in API 25 so a launcher could ask for a circular bitmap; an adaptive
    icon makes it redundant, because the launcher masks these layers into
    whatever shape it wants — circle, squircle, rounded square — and Google's
    own guidance is to drop it once you ship one. A launcher that looks for it
    falls back to android:icon, which is this.

    -anydpi-v26 rather than plain -anydpi: it is the convention every tool
    expects, and it costs nothing when every device is v26 or later.
-->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@color/ic_launcher_background" />
    <foreground android:drawable="@drawable/ic_launcher_foreground" />
    <monochrome android:drawable="@drawable/ic_launcher_monochrome" />
</adaptive-icon>
